\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Qualitative examples of the deployment rule. Each column corresponds to one dataset; the three rows show the raw image, the gating+fusion error map, and the DCD error map. White denotes true positives, red false negatives, and green false positives; black denotes background, and the yellow box marks the same region across the three rows. OCTA-500 and TopoMortar illustrate cases where DCD improves Dice or HD95; HRF and TYRE show the corresponding trade-off and failure cases. These examples are illustrative; the dataset-level quantitative comparison is in Table~\ref {tab:dcd_ablation}.}}{7}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dcd_deployment}{{4}{7}{Qualitative examples of the deployment rule. Each column corresponds to one dataset; the three rows show the raw image, the gating+fusion error map, and the DCD error map. White denotes true positives, red false negatives, and green false positives; black denotes background, and the yellow box marks the same region across the three rows. OCTA-500 and TopoMortar illustrate cases where DCD improves Dice or HD95; HRF and TYRE show the corresponding trade-off and failure cases. These examples are illustrative; the dataset-level quantitative comparison is in Table~\ref {tab:dcd_ablation}}{figure.caption.13}{}}
